WEBVTT

01:57.033 --> 01:59.494
Ordinarily, I would meet you
at Haneda airport--

01:59.577 --> 02:01.162
No problem.

02:02.330 --> 02:04.124
This is my country's military base.

02:06.417 --> 02:09.045
We're meeting again much sooner
than expected, huh?

02:17.929 --> 02:20.473
Yujiro Hanma is the brute strength pro

02:20.557 --> 02:24.060
who's said to have military might
that surpasses that of major countries.

02:24.144 --> 02:28.565
In the near future, he is going to be
involved in an incident.

02:29.274 --> 02:32.569
I would like us
to assist in this incident.

02:33.153 --> 02:37.949
Naturally, the Tokyo Metropolitan Police
Department is aware of Yujiro Hanma.

02:38.658 --> 02:43.079
But Ogre possesses nation-level might,
so who on Earth would do something to him?

02:43.663 --> 02:44.831
His son.

02:47.125 --> 02:52.088
I see. That super-boy
who kidnapped Mr. Bosch, huh?

02:52.755 --> 02:54.841
The kidnapper from that incident?!

02:54.924 --> 02:57.844
You mean that boy
who snatched the President

02:57.927 --> 03:01.681
right in front of everyone while he was
under a level-five security alert?

03:02.182 --> 03:08.104
In other words, that boy's strength is
approaching that of nation-level.

03:08.938 --> 03:13.151
But there's still something
I cannot comprehend.

03:13.818 --> 03:16.905
I realize they are both
as powerful as nations,

03:16.988 --> 03:20.200
but really, this is just a row
between father and son, right?

03:20.283 --> 03:23.912
I mean, can't we just leave them be?

03:23.995 --> 03:26.748
Can't we just let them do as they please?

03:27.498 --> 03:28.374
Right?

03:28.458 --> 03:29.626
Stop!

03:30.335 --> 03:32.170
You mustn't say more.

03:33.421 --> 03:34.631
I want you to see this.

03:36.424 --> 03:38.134
This is my guardian angel.

03:38.218 --> 03:39.636
What is it?

03:39.719 --> 03:40.720
Tar.

03:41.221 --> 03:43.097
You mean coal?

03:43.640 --> 03:47.143
To be precise, it's coal dust.

03:47.894 --> 03:52.148
I asked Ogre to do this, and he complied.

03:54.234 --> 03:56.903
It's nothing to be surprised at.

03:56.986 --> 03:59.656
After all, I am the President of the...

04:02.200 --> 04:04.661
Got any other requests, President?

04:04.744 --> 04:06.663
DEMOCRATIC PEOPLE'S PARTY

04:07.664 --> 04:10.708
<i>Three brawny men were on their knees.</i>

04:11.251 --> 04:13.670
<i>No, to be more precise,</i>

04:14.504 --> 04:17.173
<i>the three men, all three of them,</i>

04:18.383 --> 04:19.926
<i>were unconscious.</i>

04:20.802 --> 04:22.929
All three of them were expressionless.

04:23.846 --> 04:25.431
<i>Their expressions seemed to say</i>

04:26.140 --> 04:29.435
<i>that they weren't even aware
they were unconscious.</i>

04:30.770 --> 04:33.231
<i>Yujiro Hanma was in this room.</i>

04:33.856 --> 04:35.483
<i>What did this situation imply?</i>

04:37.568 --> 04:40.196
<i>This man does not sneak in.</i>

04:41.197 --> 04:45.285
<i>The heads of state gathered there
could only silently accept it.</i>

04:45.785 --> 04:50.665
<i>It meant that the security
surrounding them had been wiped out.</i>

04:51.874 --> 04:56.087
"I asked Ogre to do this,
and he complied."

04:59.424 --> 05:00.341
Ozma.

05:00.425 --> 05:03.970
You misunderstand me. I simply...

05:09.934 --> 05:12.103
<i>What a remarkable presence.</i>

05:12.687 --> 05:15.773
<i>So he is the real Ogre.</i>

05:18.735 --> 05:20.153
Put out your right hand.

05:20.236 --> 05:21.612
What?

05:39.213 --> 05:42.633
That oath you made to me
with your hand on the Bible...

05:45.345 --> 05:47.889
Repeat it to me now before God.

05:55.980 --> 05:56.898
I...

05:57.774 --> 05:58.775
I swear

05:59.317 --> 06:01.444
that the United States of America

06:01.527 --> 06:05.031
will have an amicable relationship
with Master Yujiro Hanma.

06:05.114 --> 06:09.660
We will respect you, and we will never
interfere with your life--

06:09.744 --> 06:10.661
That part!

06:12.747 --> 06:15.625
How dare you people,
who have nothing to do with my life,

06:15.708 --> 06:18.920
go sticking your noses
into a fight between me and my son?

06:20.171 --> 06:23.633
And though you're part of the government,

06:23.716 --> 06:27.970
you get together to try and meddle
in an ordinary citizen's domestic issues.

06:29.263 --> 06:32.934
Are you people trying
to pick a fight with my family?

06:33.017 --> 06:33.935
No!

06:35.019 --> 06:38.523
Ogre, please allow me to say one thing.

06:39.524 --> 06:42.985
"Ordinary citizens," "domestic problems,"
"a fight between father and son,"

06:43.069 --> 06:46.114
those phrases are far too modest.

06:46.197 --> 06:49.075
A conflict between you two is like
a conflict between nations.

06:49.158 --> 06:51.494
In other words, it's equivalent to a war!

06:52.286 --> 06:54.080
So, due to this,

06:54.163 --> 06:58.960
we must protect the people,
regardless of race!

07:04.465 --> 07:09.470
Now that you've abandoned God,
you finally tell the truth.

07:12.056 --> 07:14.767
Make absolutely sure
you stay out of my sight.

07:29.115 --> 07:30.950
Kaiser, why have you come to Japan?

07:31.033 --> 07:34.620
There's no title match, so what's
a big promoter like yourself doing here?

07:36.205 --> 07:38.166
I've come to take up a fight.

07:38.249 --> 07:40.877
A fight? You're a promoter. Why you?

07:40.960 --> 07:42.295
With whom?

07:42.378 --> 07:44.797
Who picked a fight with you, Kaiser?

07:45.465 --> 07:47.383
CENTER BOXING GYM

07:56.476 --> 07:58.686
How long has he been like that?

07:58.769 --> 08:01.355
For two hours. The whole time.

08:01.856 --> 08:04.984
No jumping rope, no shadow boxing,
no punching the sandbag.

08:05.067 --> 08:07.403
Nothing except facing the wall
in a horse stance.

08:07.487 --> 08:08.404
Is that okay?

08:08.946 --> 08:10.990
Of course it's not, Chairman!

08:11.073 --> 08:13.409
I tried to teach him a lesson
through sparring,

08:13.493 --> 08:15.119
but nobody can beat him.

08:16.496 --> 08:18.581
Mani got knocked out with one punch.

08:18.664 --> 08:21.375
Even the heavyweight Gary got busted up.

08:21.459 --> 08:23.961
Nobody wants to fight him anymore.

08:24.045 --> 08:26.005
Well, at least not within Japan.

08:26.506 --> 08:28.925
We've got a hell of a problem
on our hands.

08:36.974 --> 08:38.434
No way!

08:41.229 --> 08:42.939
This is just a puny gym...

08:43.731 --> 08:44.941
What's Kaiser doing here?

08:56.077 --> 08:57.286
Mr. Kaiser...

08:57.370 --> 08:58.329
Shut up!

08:59.997 --> 09:01.457
Beautiful.

09:01.541 --> 09:05.294
When that knucklehead Gary told me,
I wasn't convinced,

09:05.378 --> 09:06.963
but seeing him, I understand.

09:08.047 --> 09:09.966
I've been in this business 40 years,

09:10.716 --> 09:14.971
but I've never once seen lats like those.

09:15.805 --> 09:17.265
Your name's Sea King, right?

09:17.348 --> 09:18.975
Can we talk for a sec?

09:21.561 --> 09:22.812
Keep quiet!

09:23.813 --> 09:26.232
If you're gonna interfere
with training, then scram!

09:34.323 --> 09:38.160
Would it be possible to ask you a favor?

09:38.244 --> 09:39.203
Just one.

09:40.288 --> 09:42.206
Show me your strength.

09:42.832 --> 09:46.502
Instead of brushing me off,
do you think you can show me?

10:02.852 --> 10:04.061
<i>Just a single hand?</i>

10:04.562 --> 10:08.691
<i>Will he knock around a sandbag
using the largest glove they've got?</i>

10:08.774 --> 10:10.860
<i>His style is pretty ordinary.</i>

10:14.363 --> 10:17.658
<i>Shadow boxing? A practice punch?
A show of form?</i>

10:26.208 --> 10:28.377
<i>Beautiful.</i>

10:31.714 --> 10:35.217
<i>Was this the only thing I could do?
Was this really it?</i>

10:36.385 --> 10:38.137
<i>Why did I choose that glove?</i>

10:38.721 --> 10:43.601
<i>The biggest, oldest, most damaged glove...</i>

10:44.352 --> 10:46.562
<i>Why didn't I choose the newest glove?</i>

10:47.396 --> 10:49.231
<i>Because it's easy to destroy.</i>

10:49.732 --> 10:53.986
<i>This glove that had been damaged
by sweat and punches was easy to destroy.</i>

10:54.987 --> 10:55.905
<i>How cowardly.</i>

10:58.949 --> 11:03.162
<i>No matter how much Retsu
criticized his own decision,</i>

11:03.746 --> 11:05.414
<i>the boxers understood.</i>

11:06.582 --> 11:08.834
<i>They understood to their cores.</i>

11:10.211 --> 11:11.671
<i>Gloves cannot tear.</i>

11:12.713 --> 11:14.632
<i>Even when used until they're worn out,</i>

11:15.257 --> 11:18.177
<i>gloves made from genuine leather
will never yield.</i>

11:18.678 --> 11:22.598
B... Beautiful!

11:23.307 --> 11:26.894
<i>I must quit boxing. Today...</i>

11:29.230 --> 11:30.189
My apologies.

11:30.940 --> 11:32.692
That was nothing more than a trick.

11:33.234 --> 11:35.069
It has nothing to do with strength.

11:36.946 --> 11:38.364
Any one of you will do.

11:39.740 --> 11:42.118
Can any of you do what he just did?

11:44.704 --> 11:46.747
To pierce a glove with a punch.

11:47.331 --> 11:51.377
Every boxer understands
just how incredibly difficult that is.

11:52.461 --> 11:54.672
The glove is the symbol of boxing,

11:55.214 --> 11:57.383
but he's destroyed it.

11:59.719 --> 12:01.137
War!

12:01.971 --> 12:03.889
That's right. This means war.

12:03.973 --> 12:09.103
Two men put on gloves and have a contest
of strength using just their fists.

12:09.603 --> 12:12.273
The rules are simple,
profound and supreme.

12:12.898 --> 12:15.901
The Queensberry Rules,
established 150 years ago.

12:17.236 --> 12:20.990
Those 150 years were just trampled on.

12:21.741 --> 12:24.160
At the hands of 4,000 years of China.

12:24.952 --> 12:26.412
That's ridiculous. I simply--

12:26.495 --> 12:29.165
Shut up, Sea King Retsu!

12:29.832 --> 12:32.293
I'm talking dozens of millions of dollars.

12:32.376 --> 12:33.919
Don't you want it?

12:34.003 --> 12:35.963
What's the meaning of this?
Are you insult--

12:36.046 --> 12:40.926
Also, there'll be monsters
that'll make you wanna run away.

12:43.637 --> 12:45.598
The look in your eyes has changed.

12:45.681 --> 12:49.185
I knew you were a warrior.
I want you to leave this to me.

12:49.268 --> 12:51.562
One-hundred and fifty or 4,000 years.

12:52.104 --> 12:55.691
The world will leap
at the hopeless match between these two.

12:57.568 --> 13:01.822
You will fight just as you are,
not as the boxer Sea King Retsu.

13:01.906 --> 13:04.200
Just as you are, Sea King Retsu,

13:04.283 --> 13:07.703
the intruder representing
those 4,000 years of Chinese kung fu.

13:08.454 --> 13:10.706
I want you just as you are,
Sea King Retsu!

13:10.790 --> 13:14.710
Naturally this won't be
an official match, but an exhibition.

13:15.628 --> 13:17.254
I can see it.

13:17.338 --> 13:21.008
The great fighters who've fought
many fights bowing down before you.

13:21.091 --> 13:24.804
Yet, there's no belt around your waist.

13:25.513 --> 13:27.723
Even without it, the world knows.

13:28.516 --> 13:31.227
The belt around your waist
that cannot be seen.

13:32.394 --> 13:34.230
How come it can't be seen?

13:34.897 --> 13:36.982
Because it's so damn bright!

13:37.942 --> 13:41.654
<i>The wheels of fate had been
almost stopped, almost tossed away...</i>

13:42.196 --> 13:44.532
<i>Until they met
the exceptional force of Kaiser.</i>

13:47.076 --> 13:48.994
<i>They began to spin again.</i>

13:49.078 --> 13:51.914
Mr. Retsu, I want you to accompany me.

13:53.999 --> 13:55.376
To the States!

13:57.127 --> 14:00.172
<i>Why am I going too?</i>

14:12.726 --> 14:15.437
<i>Like I figured, Dad.</i>

14:20.860 --> 14:21.944
Bacon and eggs.

14:22.736 --> 14:23.946
Miso soup with seaweed.

14:24.572 --> 14:25.948
Grilled salted Pacific saury.

14:26.574 --> 14:27.950
A pile of shredded cabbage.

14:29.076 --> 14:30.703
Such a hearty breakfast.

14:50.055 --> 14:51.307
You know...

14:52.057 --> 14:54.768
Isn't this miso soup salty?

14:56.061 --> 14:58.480
Huh? Why?

15:00.107 --> 15:01.859
I'm the one who'd like to know.

15:03.068 --> 15:06.363
You're the one who cooked this, Dad.

15:11.327 --> 15:14.079
I do appreciate that you made it for me,

15:14.705 --> 15:16.248
but you asked me how it was.

15:18.834 --> 15:21.837
No sense of taste? This is home cooking.

15:22.379 --> 15:24.757
Your family decides
whether it's good or not.

15:37.102 --> 15:38.270
So it goes.

15:38.854 --> 15:42.775
That's how it starts, an ordinary fight
between father and son.

15:48.197 --> 15:49.031
What is it?

15:49.907 --> 15:51.784
Who's staying here?

15:54.036 --> 15:58.040
Oh, I get it. Please, have a look around
inside until you're satisfied.

16:01.001 --> 16:02.044
Forget it.

16:05.714 --> 16:09.218
If you're that worried about me,
you should come and stay over more.

16:11.261 --> 16:12.096
I will.

16:20.521 --> 16:21.438
<i>This is no good.</i>

16:22.815 --> 16:25.526
<i>I'm solid... A total solid.</i>

16:26.694 --> 16:28.028
<i>There's still muscle left.</i>

16:29.488 --> 16:31.156
<i>My muscles haven't melted.</i>

16:34.952 --> 16:35.786
<i>Liquefy...</i>

16:37.663 --> 16:40.416
<i>Liquefy my muscles.</i>

16:44.294 --> 16:46.964
<i>Well, well. Long time no see.</i>

16:47.923 --> 16:48.966
<i>Teacher.</i>

16:51.593 --> 16:53.012
<i>I'm very sorry</i>,

16:53.721 --> 16:57.808
<i>but my strength
still hasn't come close to yours.</i>

16:59.727 --> 17:03.981
<i>Just when did I start to learn from you?</i>

17:06.025 --> 17:08.485
<i>Your physical ability is full of mystery.</i>

17:09.111 --> 17:11.780
<i>A bewitching treasure chest of dynamics.</i>

17:12.740 --> 17:16.076
<i>Your history is filled
with hatred and rejection.</i>

17:17.327 --> 17:18.495
<i>However...</i>

17:19.329 --> 17:22.249
<i>Among all the beings on Earth
that strive for speed,</i>

17:23.042 --> 17:25.085
<i>you are a rare one,</i>

17:25.169 --> 17:28.756
<i>the one and only that can go
immediately from zero to max speed.</i>

17:29.339 --> 17:32.509
<i>There's no need to accelerate.
You start off at max speed.</i>

17:33.135 --> 17:38.640
<i>And its speed,
if it were the size of a human,</i>

17:40.059 --> 17:43.520
<i>it would travel at an amazing 270 kph.</i>

17:44.188 --> 17:47.024
<i>Do you have any idea
how great an achievement that is?</i>

17:47.941 --> 17:52.071
<i>If a human wanted
to start running at 270 kph...</i>

17:52.738 --> 17:55.532
<i>Right. They'd have to do it like this.</i>

17:56.158 --> 17:58.035
<i>In other words, they'd die.</i>

17:58.869 --> 18:01.705
<i>It's not a level that can be achieved
with muscle fibers,</i>

18:01.789 --> 18:03.540
<i>a height that cannot be reached...</i>

18:04.416 --> 18:05.417
<i>That's not true!</i>

18:06.251 --> 18:08.253
<i>One day I saw your corpse.</i>

18:09.004 --> 18:10.172
<i>What?!</i>

18:10.756 --> 18:12.091
<i>That was a huge clue.</i>

18:12.883 --> 18:15.427
<i>Not muscle. Not fiber.</i>

18:16.261 --> 18:18.722
<i>Your insides were a milky white liquid.</i>

18:19.264 --> 18:23.977
<i>What supported that 270-kph start
wasn't sturdy muscle fibers.</i>

18:26.146 --> 18:27.189
<i>It was liquid.</i>

18:46.959 --> 18:48.710
Have I come close to you now?

18:54.091 --> 18:57.344
You haven't said a word
since you arrived in Vegas.

18:57.427 --> 19:01.598
Sea King Retsu,
don't tell me that you're dissatisfied

19:01.682 --> 19:04.309
with the special suite I booked for you.

19:05.477 --> 19:07.479
I have been thinking as well.

19:08.230 --> 19:12.484
What is it that I dislike
about this city devoted to extravagance?

19:12.568 --> 19:14.653
Like I figured, you don't like it.

19:15.404 --> 19:16.780
I've come to my conclusion.

19:17.281 --> 19:19.408
I think I can guess what it is.

19:21.118 --> 19:22.870
There is nothing real in this city.

19:23.370 --> 19:25.873
There is not a single thing
that is authentic.

19:26.582 --> 19:30.544
All these artificial things
in this barren desert,

19:30.627 --> 19:33.130
and the passion and effort
required to build this city,

19:33.797 --> 19:35.591
I cannot help but admire them.

19:35.674 --> 19:36.633
But still,

19:37.426 --> 19:39.136
everything in this city is fake.

19:39.803 --> 19:43.891
Everywhere you look, there is foliage
that couldn't possibly grow here.

19:44.641 --> 19:46.393
Structures like those of a great city.

19:46.977 --> 19:48.145
A fake Statue of Liberty.

19:48.729 --> 19:50.147
A fake Eiffel Tower.

19:50.731 --> 19:52.149
A fake Arc de Triomphe.

19:52.733 --> 19:54.151
A fake Sphinx.

19:54.818 --> 19:56.153
A fake Pyramid.

19:56.236 --> 19:59.406
However, all these fakes are top quality.

19:59.990 --> 20:02.409
Sea King Retsu, if they were all genuine,

20:02.492 --> 20:05.579
if they were all the real deal,
would that satisfy you?

20:07.497 --> 20:09.374
In this world, Sea King Retsu,

20:09.458 --> 20:13.503
there are plenty of third-rate things
that claim they're the real deal.

20:13.587 --> 20:17.549
In fact, there are probably more of those.

20:18.091 --> 20:21.470
Inferior products that have built
legends as the real deal.

20:21.553 --> 20:23.472
You can't say you've never seen them.

20:27.059 --> 20:28.936
Oh, now, now.

20:29.019 --> 20:32.522
I see. It's probably as you say, Kaiser.

20:33.023 --> 20:36.693
There's an astounding number
of imitators in kung fu as well.

20:37.402 --> 20:41.406
Crude fighting styles that only exist
because they were pointlessly handed down.

20:42.783 --> 20:44.534
The city of fakes.

20:49.289 --> 20:51.583
Hey! You sure you wanna do that?

20:52.251 --> 20:54.962
If I drink this,
I won't get into the ring.

20:55.587 --> 20:58.548
When you do, show 'em the Drunken Fist.

21:17.567 --> 21:19.403
Amazing.

21:19.486 --> 21:22.322
He's a former champion,
so of course I know about him.

21:22.406 --> 21:25.909
But seeing him for real,
he's a way bigger deal than I imagined.

21:25.993 --> 21:27.077
What's his size?

21:27.160 --> 21:31.498
He's 237 cm tall, 151 kilos.

21:36.586 --> 21:38.171
He got in the ring!

21:43.593 --> 21:45.595
Ladies and gentlemen.

21:46.096 --> 21:47.556
It has been 150 years

21:47.639 --> 21:52.311
since the Queensberry Rules
were established.

21:52.978 --> 21:55.188
And now modern boxing
faces its greatest crisis.

21:55.272 --> 21:57.524
Its most powerful foe has arrived.

22:02.112 --> 22:08.035
In the 4,001st year of kung fu,
one finally claims to be the Dragon.

22:08.660 --> 22:10.954
Sea King Retsu!
